   "question": "Complete `steps_for_tol` and `adaptive_rk4`.",
   "widget": {
    "kind": "code",
    "language": "python",
    "prelude": "import numpy as np\ndef rk4(f, t0, y0, h, n):\n    t, y = t0, np.array(y0, dtype=float)\n    for _ in range(n):\n        k1 = f(t, y); k2 = f(t + h / 2, y + h / 2 * k1); k3 = f(t + h / 2, y + h / 2 * k2); k4 = f(t + h, y + h * k3)\n        y = y + h / 6 * (k1 + 2 * k2 + 2 * k3 + k4); t += h\n    return y\ndef euler(f, t0, y0, h, n):\n    t, y = t0, np.array(y0, dtype=float)\n    for _ in range(n):\n        y = y + h * f(t, y); t += h\n    return y\n",
    "starter": "import numpy as np\n\n# rk4(f, t0, y0, h, n) and euler(f, t0, y0, h, n) are provided; both return y at t0 + n*h.\n\ndef steps_for_tol(method, f, y0, T, exact, tol, p):\n    \"\"\"Run method with n0 = 10 steps, read C = error / h**p from the first\n    component, and return the smallest n with C * (T / n)**p <= tol.\"\"\"\n    ...\n\ndef adaptive_rk4(f, t0, y0, T, tol, h=0.1):\n    \"\"\"Step-doubling RK4. Return (y at T, accepted steps).\"\"\"\n    ...\n",
    "solution": "import math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef steps_for_tol(method, f, y0, T, exact, tol, p):\n    h = T / 10\n    err = abs(np.atleast_1d(method(f, 0.0, y0, h, 10))[0] - exact)\n    C = err / h ** p\n    return math.ceil(T / (tol / C) ** (1 / p))\n\ndef adaptive_rk4(f, t0, y0, T, tol, h=0.1):\n    t, y, accepted = t0, np.array(y0, dtype=float), 0\n    while t < T - 1e-15:\n        h = min(h, T - t)\n        big = rk4(f, t, y, h, 1)\n        half = rk4(f, t + h / 2, rk4(f, t, y, h / 2, 1), h / 2, 1)\n        err = float(np.max(np.abs(half - big))) / 15\n        scale = tol * max(1.0, float(np.max(np.abs(half))))\n        if err <= scale:\n            t += h\n            y = half + (half - big) / 15\n            accepted += 1\n        h = h * (5.0 if err == 0 else min(5.0, max(0.2, 0.9 * (scale / err) ** 0.2)))\n    return y, accepted\n",
